Kenner Gordon wrote:
>
> The Rosetta Stone would be the new archeologist quest artifact, with a
> luckstone as its base item. When read or invoked, it wouldy identify
> all spellbooks and scrolls in your inventory.

Identifying books and scrolls is not a particularly useful feature. 
There are enough identify scrolls that by the time I get to the Quest I
have often identified most scrolls and books by type.  Many games have
enough altars that by the time I get to the Quest I know the BUC state
of my important books and scrolls.

There are two features that might be powerful -

Invoke it to read a book with guaranteed success.  It would be a bit
like a source of holy water but not quite.  A blessed book can be read
with guaranteed success every single time until it wears out but this
would only work as often as the invocation timer allows.

Invoke it to read a book without increasing the read count so it does
not wear out.  Powerfull in an endurance game.  Pointless in a race
ascension.


